Export the complete results of a run as one JSON document.

The document holds the run exactly as the service described it, and every
evaluated row beneath it: the item that was evaluated, what the target
answered, and each evaluator's score, verdict and reason.

This is the machine-readable path. `azd ai eval run output list` is the readable one.
Derive any other shape from this file.

Usage
  azd ai eval run output export [run] [flags]

Flags
      --eval string             : Name of the eval declared in the configuration, or its id.
      --force                   : Replace an output file that already exists.
      --format string           : Output format. Only json is supported. (default "json")
      --output-file string      : Write the document to this path. Required; pass - to write to stdout.
      --path string             : Directory holding azure.eval.yaml. Defaults to the path init used, then ./evals.
      --project-endpoint string : Foundry project endpoint.
      --run string              : Run to act on. Defaults to the last run recorded for --eval.

Global Flags
  -C, --cwd string         : Sets the current working directory
      --debug              : Enables debug and diagnostics logging
  -e, --environment string : The name of the environment to use
  -h, --help               : help for export
      --no-prompt          : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
  -o, --output string      : The output format (default "default")

Examples
  Export the latest run and all its evaluated rows
    azd ai eval run output export --eval quality --output-file results.json

  Convert the exported items to JSONL with jq
    jq -c '.items[]' results.json > results.jsonl
